Q3. Explain Runtime Polymorphism using

Animal a = new Dog();

Interview Ready Answer

Runtime Polymorphism is achieved when a parent
reference points to a child object.

Example

Animal a=new Dog();

Internal Working

Step 1

Compiler checks reference type.

Animal has sound().

↓

Step 2

Heap memory allocated.

↓

Step 3

Dog object created.

↓

Step 4

Reference variable a stores Dog object's address.

↓

Step 5

When

a.sound();

is executed,

Compiler allows the call because Animal contains
sound().

↓

JVM follows the reference to the actual object.

↓

Actual object is Dog.

↓

Dog overrides sound().

↓

Dog.sound() executes.

This runtime decision is called

Dynamic Method Dispatch.

Memory

Stack                     Heap

a ---------------------> Dog Object

Key Point

Reference Type

↓

Compile-Time

Actual Object

↓

Runtime

