Q4. Can Runtime Polymorphism be achieved using
static, private and final methods?

Interview Ready Answer

No.

Runtime Polymorphism depends on Method Overriding.

If overriding is not possible,

Runtime Polymorphism is not possible.

------------------------------------------------------------

static Method

Cannot be overridden.

It is Method Hiding.

Resolved by Compiler.

No Runtime Polymorphism.

------------------------------------------------------------

private Method

Not inherited.

Cannot be overridden.

No Runtime Polymorphism.

------------------------------------------------------------

final Method

Cannot be overridden.

No Runtime Polymorphism.

Memory Trick

No Overriding

↓

No Runtime Polymorphism

